From 1d885840dd274a0855c2671057be1023bc0d7ae6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:56:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: enable RTD3 on MacBookPro15,1

Hello everyone,

On the MacBookPro15,1, both JHL7540 Titan Ridge NHIs and their host
routers remain active in D0 while idle. The machine uses the software
connection manager, where runtime PM is currently only enabled for USB4
routers. The two idle Thunderbolt domains account for approximately 3 W
of otherwise avoidable system power consumption.

Our earlier patch "xhci-pci: keep Titan Ridge active on
MacBookPro15,1" addressed a separate problem in the same topology. The
Titan Ridge xHCI controllers lose USB 3 connect events after entering D3
under Apple's OSDW firmware path and therefore need to remain in D0.
That restriction does not apply to the NHIs.

So this patch enables RTD3 for the Titan Ridge 4C NHIs on this model.
Both NHIs then runtime-suspend to D3hot while the separate xHCI
controllers remain active in D0. USB 3 hotplug and repeated suspend and
resume cycles continue to work.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260730210655.15514-1-dev@deq.rocks/
Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c | 8 ++++++++
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h | 3 +++
 drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c  | 5 +++--
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
index 6d0c9d3..1790df5 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/errno.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
+#include <linux/dmi.h>
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
@@ -1186,6 +1187,13 @@ static void nhi_check_quirks(struct tb_nhi *nhi)
 			 */
 			nhi->quirks |= QUIRK_E2E;
 			break;
+		case PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_4C_NHI:
+			if (dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "MacBookPro15,1")) {
+				nhi->quirks |= QUIRK_FORCE_RTD3;
+				pci_info(nhi->pdev,
+					 "enabling RTD3 for Apple T2 Titan Ridge NHI\n");
+			}
+			break;
 		}
 	}
 }
diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
index 24ac424..69bc502 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
@@ -50,6 +50,9 @@ struct tb_nhi_ops {
 
 extern const struct tb_nhi_ops icl_nhi_ops;
 
+/* Host interface quirks shared with the connection manager. */
+#define QUIRK_FORCE_RTD3	BIT(2)
+
 /*
  * PCI IDs used in this driver from Win Ridge forward. There is no
  * need for the PCI quirk anymore as we will use ICM also on Apple
diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
index 1b4ff0d..5f83de7 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
@@ -3003,8 +3003,9 @@ static int tb_start(struct tb *tb, bool reset)
 	 * implement the necessary router operations.
 	 */
 	tb->root_switch->no_nvm_upgrade = !tb_switch_is_usb4(tb->root_switch);
-	/* All USB4 routers support runtime PM */
-	tb->root_switch->rpm = tb_switch_is_usb4(tb->root_switch);
+	/* USB4 routers and quirked NHIs support runtime PM */
+	tb->root_switch->rpm = tb_switch_is_usb4(tb->root_switch) ||
+			       (tb->nhi->quirks & QUIRK_FORCE_RTD3);
 
 	ret = tb_switch_configure(tb->root_switch);
 	if (ret) {
-- 
